es not match.","related":["IDEA-L13","IDEA-L18"],"related_status":"conjectural","status":"partial","title":"Successive observations of one carrier chain"}
{"alternatives":"Calling a static intersection of block definitions a realised overlap, or calling a partial family a cover.","description":"Potential overlap is a nonempty intersection of fixed blocks. Realised overlap also requires a present shared constituent.","expressive":"Potential overlap is a function of the block definitions. Realised overlap is a function of those definitions and the present edges. Neither is a new coordinate.","feasibility":"active_intersection and labelled_active_blocks use potential overlap of the blocks that contain a present edge. realised_intersection, labelled_realised_blocks, and realised_overlap_count are fixture maps and are not a frozen round. block_family_report classifies the fixed family and does not read a state.","formulation":"docs/cover-observations.md. A nonempty intersection of two blocks is potential overlap. A nonempty intersection of those blocks with the present edges is realised overlap. A family whose union is not the carrier is a partial family. A full cover, a partition, an overlapping cover, a nested family, and a dynamically active subfamily are different.","idea_id":"IDEA-L21","methods":"src/rrc/composition.py. The path comparison remains a fixture. It is not a frozen cell. Atlas-011 omission lists are partial families. The stored plans were not rewritten. tests/test_composition.py separates a present shared edge from a fixed intersection. The triangle and path numbers are fixtures. A block family that changes over time is not implemented. Atlas-014 used one realised-overlap count as the first map of one successive item. That item is not the overlap sample. The idea stays partial. Atlas-015 stored twenty observations of the chain cover [(0,1),(1,2)] and [(1,2),(2,3)]. The idea stays partial.","phenomena":"A state can make two blocks active while every shared edge is absent. The active-block maps still record the fixed intersection.","related":["IDEA-L08","IDEA-L19"],"related_status":"conjectural","status":"pa