{"alternatives":"Adding a disconnected bit that never changes a pair-toggle weight, or reading a derived label as independent state.","description":"A derived coordinate is a function of the pair state. An independent coordinate can differ while the pair state stays the same.","expressive":"Class D is a coordinate defined as a function of the pair state. The two-bit count is in this class. Class I in this fixture is a third bit that is not a function of the two pair bits. Once the bit is listed, the state is ordinary pair state of a larger carrier. It is not a new event type.","feasibility":"rrc-0.4.0 compiles current-state weights on single toggles. Two values of one extra listed bit can change a pair-toggle weight and still be that grammar. A joint two-bit event is outside the support. History at an unchanged state is outside it. No engine change is made. A freely toggling bit with no effect on the pair weights is not the witness.","formulation":"docs/compilation-gate.md. Derived maps are in src/rrc/composition.py and have new_state false. The activity rows are in src/rrc/coordinate_examples.py. An independent hyperedge that is not a listed edge, a joint two-bit event, and a history-dependent row remain outside the grammar. Coupled transitions are allowed. Independence of the two processes is not assumed.","idea_id":"IDEA-L22","methods":"src/rrc/coordinate_examples.py builds the activity rows without the compiler. tests/test_coordinate_examples.py compares those rows with compile_weight_table on the four-node chain. The pair bits do not determine the row. A free bit keeps equal probabilities. A joint two-bit step is outside the single-toggle support. The independent bit in IDEA-L16 has no witness and is not implemented. It is not a frozen cell. docs/state-event-families.md separates a derived coordinate, an extra listed bit, a joint two-bit step, an identified interface, a duplicated interface, and a changing block family. The activity table remains EQ-027. It is 