{"pattern_id":"PAT-017","kind":"analytical_distinction","status":"recorded","schedules_follow_up":false,"statement":"Single-coordinate support after recoding and exact closure after dropping inactive state are separate properties. Hidden raw-weight dependence can cancel by common scaling or remain through relative rates, even with identical support.","evidence":"docs/xor-mask-recoding.md and reports/2026-10-26-xor-recoding.md give the general proof; provenance/2026-10-26-xor-verification.json records the exact software controls. This is analytic evidence, not a frozen experimental observation."}
{"pattern_id":"PAT-018","kind":"analytical_distinction","status":"recorded","schedules_follow_up":false,"statement":"A component description sufficient for standalone aggregate prediction may omit event labels or raw scale that a specified interaction makes consequential. Labelwise weighted quotients give a sufficient preserved description for this product, including evolving hidden state.","evidence":"docs/labelled-sync-composition.md proves the scoped result; reports/2026-10-26-sync-composition.md and provenance/2026-10-26-sync-verification.json separate proofs, exact counterexamples and software validation. Zero new scientific cells."}
{"pattern_id":"PAT-019","kind":"analytical_distinction","status":"recorded","schedules_follow_up":false,"statement":"The context class and observer determine which label and weight distinctions must survive abstraction. Shared labels can be separated individually; private names can be merged for fixed-H state-only contexts, but private event weight, even inside a constant observation, competes with a partner's move.","evidence":"docs/contextual-preservation.md proves an exact rich-context criterion and finite separators; reports/2026-10-26-contextual-preservation.md and provenance/2026-10-26-context-verification.json distinguish the general proof, boundary counterexamples and bounded software validation. Zero new scientific cells."}
{"pattern_id":"PAT-020","kind":"analytical_distinction","status":"recorded","schedules_follow_up":false,"statement":"A closed predictive observation may lose the inherited interface needed for later composition. Shared-port target agreement is separately required for copies to remain consistent; enforcing agreement can change normalised dynamics even when the components have equal port marginals.","evidence":"docs/shared-changing-port.md gives the general support/type proofs and a reducible dynamic feedback/null construction. reports/2026-10-26-shared-changing-port.md and provenance/2026-10-26-shared-port-verification.json separate proof, software controls and interpretation. No new scientific atlas cells."}
{"pattern_id":"PAT-021","kind":"analytical_distinction","status":"recorded","schedules_follow_up":false,"statement":"A changing attachment policy can reduce exactly to a fixed guarded protocol while its link mode remains necessary for actor-preserving prediction at active configurations. Such finite-state reducibility does not imply a same-clock one-bit support encoding; a positive switching example has a five-cycle.","evidence":"docs/switching-attachment.md gives the compiler, coarsest-refinement proof and scoped parity obstruction; reports/2026-10-26-switching-attachment.md and provenance/2026-10-26-switching-link-verification.json distinguish proofs/software controls from scientific cells. No follow-up is scheduled."}

